/*  Text — `the length of`, `the characters from … to … of`, `contains`, `starts with`, `ends with`,
    `the position of … in`, `replace … with … in`, `trimmed`, `split by`, `in uppercase` and `in
    lowercase`, `the first … characters of` and `the last … characters of`, `the current directory`, `the environment variable`,
    `is alphabetic`, `is numeric`, `is whitespace` and `the code point of`.

    ★ Each is the runtime's own call, the one `cufet build` makes, so a text is measured and cut in
      CHARACTERS — code points — and never in bytes.

    ★ `in uppercase` and `in lowercase` read the case table in the shared runtime, which the
      interpreter's table generates — so both agree by construction. The character classes are a
      table there too, for the same reason.
*/

Pull books on collections, and the c-language.
    /// Whether an expression is one of the text operations here.
    Bind fact to is-text-operation, given (the text kind):
        Return kind is "TextSubstringRange" or kind is "TextContains" or kind is "TextAffixTest" or kind is "TextFind"
            or kind is "TextReplace" or kind is "TextTrim" or kind is "TextSplit" or kind is "NumberConvert"
            or kind is "TextCase" or kind is "TextSubstringEdge" or kind is "CurrentDirectoryExpression"
            or kind is "PathCheckExpression" or kind is "EnvironmentVariableExpression"
            or kind is "CharacterTest" or kind is "CodePointOf".
    Done.

    Bind text to text-operation-kind, given (the text kind):
        If kind is "TextContains" or kind is "TextAffixTest" or kind is "PathCheckExpression" or kind is "CharacterTest", return "fact".
        If kind is "CodePointOf", return "number".
        If kind is "TextFind" or kind is "NumberConvert", return "voidable number".
        If kind is "CurrentDirectoryExpression" or kind is "EnvironmentVariableExpression", return "voidable text".
        If kind is "TextSplit", return "series of text".
        Return "text".
    Done.

    /// A text operation as C.
    Bind c-language axiom or failure to c-text-operation unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        Define kind as expression's kind.
        If kind is "TextFind":
            Define found as cast one's c-fields-in-order on (expression, 1, 2) or pass the failure off.
            Define c-language place-found, given (the c-language axiom within, the c-language axiom sought),
                as [({ int cf_fd = cufet_str_find(the within, the sought); cf_fd ? cvo_number_some(cufet_dec_from_ll(cf_fd)) : cvo_number_none(); })].
            Return cast in-order on (item 1 of found, place-found on (item 3 of found, item 2 of found)).
        Done.
        // `the current directory` — void when there is none to report.
        If kind is "CurrentDirectoryExpression":
            Return [({ const char* cf_cwd = cufet_getcwd(); cf_cwd ? cvo_text_some(cf_cwd) : cvo_text_none(); })].
        Done.
        // Those with more than one operand, each worked out in turn.
        If kind is "TextSubstringEdge" or kind is "TextContains" or kind is "TextAffixTest" or kind is "TextSplit"
                or kind is "TextReplace" or kind is "TextSubstringRange":
            Return cast one's c-text-of-several on (expression) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Define text-c as cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "TextTrim", return call-of-one on ("cufet_str_trim", text-c).
        // `the environment variable <name>` — void when it is not set.
        If kind is "EnvironmentVariableExpression":
            Define c-language variable-read, given (the c-language axiom named),
                as [({ const char* cf_ev = cufet_getenv(the named); cf_ev ? cvo_text_some(cf_ev) : cvo_text_none(); })].
            Return variable-read on (text-c).
        Done.
        // `the path … exists`, `is a directory`, `is a file`.
        If kind is "PathCheckExpression":
            Define asked as (cast field-of on (expression, 2))'s word.
            If asked is "Exists", return call-of-one on ("cufet_path_exists", text-c).
            If asked is "IsDirectory", return call-of-one on ("cufet_path_is_dir", text-c).
            If asked is "IsFile", return call-of-one on ("cufet_path_is_file", text-c).
            Return a failure (cast not-built on ("the path check {asked}")).
        Done.
        // Casing reads the shared runtime's table — the one the interpreter reads too.
        If kind is "TextCase":
            If (cast field-of on (expression, 2))'s word is "true", return call-of-one on ("cufet_str_upper", text-c).
            Return call-of-one on ("cufet_str_lower", text-c).
        Done.
        // `is alphabetic`, `is numeric`, `is whitespace` read the shared runtime's classes, as casing does.
        If kind is "CharacterTest":
            Define tested as call-of-one on ("cufet_str_{(cast field-of on (expression, 2))'s word in lowercase}", text-c).
            If (cast field-of on (expression, 3))'s word is "true", return negated on (tested).
            Return bracketed on (tested).
        Done.
        // `the code point of` — refused when it runs unless the text is one character.
        If kind is "CodePointOf":
            Define c-language code-point, given (the c-language axiom letter, the number row),
                as [({ int cf_cp = cufet_str_code_point(the letter); if (cf_cp < 0) cufet_raise(cufet_msgf("'the code point of' needs exactly one character (line the row).")); cufet_dec_from_ll(cf_cp); })].
            Return code-point on (text-c, cast line-number on (cast field-of on (expression, 2))).
        Done.
        // `converted to number` — of a text; void when it is no number.
        If kind is "NumberConvert":
            If (cast one's kind-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off) is "bits":
                Return call-of-one on ("cufet_bits_to_number", text-c).
            Done.
            Define c-language number-parsed, given (the c-language axiom written),
                as [({ CufetDec cf_pn; cufet_parse_number(the written, &cf_pn) ? cvo_number_some(cf_pn) : cvo_number_none(); })].
            Return number-parsed on (text-c).
        Done.
        Return a failure (cast not-built on (kind)).
    Done.

    /// A text operation of two or three operands as C, the operands worked out in turn.
    Bind c-language axiom or failure to c-text-of-several unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        Define kind as expression's kind.
        Define last as 2.
        If kind is "TextReplace", the last becomes 3.
        If kind is "TextSubstringRange" and cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (expression, 3)) is false, the last becomes 3.
        Define sides as cast one's c-fields-in-order on (expression, 1, last) or pass the failure off.
        Define prefix as item 1 of sides.
        Define text-c as item 2 of sides.
        Define second as item 3 of sides.
        // `the first <n> characters of`, `the last <n> characters of` — as many as there are.
        If kind is "TextSubstringEdge":
            Define c-language edge-of, given (the c-language axiom whole, the c-language axiom count, the fact from-end),
                as [cufet_str_edge(the whole, cufet_to_int(the count), the from-end)].
            Return cast in-order on (prefix, edge-of on (text-c, second, (cast field-of on (expression, 3))'s word is "true")).
        Done.
        If kind is "TextContains":
            Define c-language holds-text, given (the c-language axiom whole, the c-language axiom part), as [(strstr(the whole, the part) != NULL)].
            Return cast in-order on (prefix, holds-text on (text-c, second)).
        Done.
        If kind is "TextAffixTest":
            If (cast field-of on (expression, 3))'s word is "true", return cast in-order on (prefix, call-of-two on ("cufet_str_ends", text-c, second)).
            Return cast in-order on (prefix, call-of-two on ("cufet_str_starts", text-c, second)).
        Done.
        If kind is "TextSplit":
            Define c-language split-up, given (the c-language axiom whole, the c-language axiom separator, the number at-line),
                as [({ cser_text* cf_sp = cser_text_new(); const char** cf_parts; int cf_n = cufet_str_split(the whole, the separator, &cf_parts, the at-line); for (int cf_j = 0; cf_j < cf_n; cf_j++) cser_text_append(cf_sp, cf_parts[cf_j]); cf_sp; })].
            Return cast in-order on (prefix, split-up on (text-c, second, cast line-number on (cast field-of on (expression, 3)))).
        Done.
        If kind is "TextReplace":
            Define c-language replaced, given (the c-language axiom whole, the c-language axiom sought, the c-language axiom replacement, the number at-line),
                as [cufet_str_replace(the whole, the sought, the replacement, the at-line)].
            Return cast in-order on (prefix, replaced on (text-c, second, item 4 of sides, cast line-number on (cast field-of on (expression, 4)))).
        Done.
        // `the characters from … to … of`, to the end when there is no `to`.
        Define upto as c-verbatim on ([-1]).
        If last is 3, the upto becomes call-of-one on ("cufet_to_int", item 4 of sides).
        Define c-language ranged, given (the c-language axiom whole, the c-language axiom first-place, the c-language axiom upto, the number at-line),
            as [cufet_str_range(the whole, cufet_to_int(the first-place), the upto, the at-line)].
        Return cast in-order on (prefix, ranged on (text-c, second, upto, cast line-number on (cast field-of on (expression, 4)))).
    Done.

    /// `the length of <text>` — in characters.
    Bind c-language axiom to c-text-length, given (the c-language axiom text-c):
        Define c-language length-held, given (the c-language axiom whole), as [cufet_dec_from_ll((long long)cufet_u8_len(the whole))].
        Return length-held on (text-c).
    Done.
Done.
